# Opinion

Meeting: 0026-ensure-calendar-sync-basic-auth-and-cloud
Agent: ArchitectB
Task: ensure calendar sync basic auth and cloud
Context:
- New requirements: basic-auth registration tied to local event storage, manual sync to configured cloud server, optional OIDC, and graceful handling when the remote DB is unavailable.
- UI needs explicit sync status plus a button to trigger pulls/pushes without blocking local workflows.
Position:
- Layering sync as an adapter on top of scoped local storage keeps the CalendarModel unchanged while supporting Basic or Bearer auth paths.
- Making sync failures non-fatal preserves offline UX yet still signals risk via status messaging.
Recommendations:
- Keep scoped storage keys per user to prevent cross-account leakage.
- When OIDC is configured, require tokens for sync but allow local-only use if remote readiness fails.
- Extend remote adapter contract to accept richer auth metadata if future servers need mTLS or API keys.
